  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each expression.\n\n- Expression I is not a binomial. The polynomial ${x}^{2}+x+4$ has three terms, so it is a trinomial, not a binomial.\n\n- Expression II is a binomial. The polynomial ${x}^{3}+2x$ has two terms, so it is indeed a binomial.\n\n- Expression III is a binomial. The polynomial $2{x}^{2}+5$ has two terms, so it is indeed a binomial.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
